                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A short Metroidvania to play and enjoy, it was a fun surprice.\r\nThe good:\r\n-Art style is really good adn resembles 60's comics.\r\n-Variety of challenges on each planet.\r\n-Mostly tight controllers.\r\n\r\nThe bad:\r\n-The Solar System map drags at first.\r\n-important info is shown on NPC you don't interact with.\r\n-Wall Jump is clonky.\r\n\r\nThe Ugly:\r\n-With the exeptiion of one Music track at the first planet and the final boss, most of the music is there to fill the void.\r\n-Blaster and Sword sound effects are too loud.\r\n\r\nThe game is really good but it still has a lot of stuff to polish like no one tells you can pogo on enemies with your sword.\r\nThe game has a lot of potential and if there's a sequel I hope the expand on the character's personality and the universe she lives in.",
